From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/13] wifi: mt76: mt7615: add the MT7668's CE commands and transmit descriptor

A firmware that owns the MAC takes connections through the flat CE
commands and needs its own transmit descriptor: data goes to the lmac
port with a 44-byte append carrying the bss index, management is a
command on the mcu port, the descriptor sets the retry count and
lifetime, and a management frame without a rate from mac80211 uses the
band's lowest basic rate.

Add both in new files, the commands as an mt7615_mcu_ops table: the
firmware handles block ack, the station table and power state, so the
host only raises and drops the BSS. Nothing uses them yet.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt76_connac_mcu.h	2026-08-09 14:25:30
+++ b/mt76_connac_mcu.h	2026-09-21 12:00:00
@@ -1331,8 +1331,13 @@
